#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124433 :question/id #uuid "c1120305-c8cb-5f57-97b1-9b31dc059b4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9961" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\det(A) = 0$\n\nII. $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible \n\n$$\n\\qquad \\Leftrightarrow \\qquad \\left\\{\\; \\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{n} \\\\ & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\mathbf{0}\\} \\\\ & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned} \\right.\n$$\n\n\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\det(A) = 0.$* $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nSince $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ must be invertible, which means $\\det(A) \\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n.$* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673152 :question-generator/id #uuid "98d1ae0f-fe25-5f83-ad3e-b1ca1abf1507" :question-generator/script "generators/2a/2a945fe3732d4408a16a7570b7fa320c2020c00b82597e4e5a237b5bcdd28d14/17592186124629.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bec134f4-8ac1-5fd3-a994-79031801df9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123603} {:answer/id #uuid "e52ece27-d671-527d-aac5-dac055efd06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123604} {:answer/id #uuid "2e01b189-5d9a-582b-a3da-d616b84586a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123605} {:answer/id #uuid "32960b14-b04a-59a2-9224-0b8a82626700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123606} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffd9fe3-d1f5-5a30-b5aa-c6b01c0e6506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123607}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9eda024b-b844-536e-bf1a-f1efd2375bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123602}] :question/id #uuid "f935b331-7ef7-5abb-b2c6-c78c4160f9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-47586" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n> *If $A$ is a $n \\times n$ matrix and $det(A) \\ne 0$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n1. $A$ has no inverse\n2. $Null(A)$ has no basis\n3. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06680c4f-a621-5dc3-875e-3896db2af04b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460023} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1cf54f-05d3-5550-8f3d-cdfa3137d5bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06680c4f-a621-5dc3-875e-3896db2af04b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460023} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3156979-45c5-5d24-80c1-f665fce48ba8" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c8b9c9-048e-580b-90b5-0615fcacbfe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460025} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd76941-0308-57d6-9b7b-3ba6c48171e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cd76941-0308-57d6-9b7b-3ba6c48171e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460026} :answer-field/id #uuid "44325e4a-3b71-5949-9822-a4ed24085c3a" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{7}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3989b63d-47f8-5757-bb11-6a685f029eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460027} {:answer/id #uuid "16bc9a89-2517-5c10-b196-866970cad27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3989b63d-47f8-5757-bb11-6a685f029eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460027} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9665add-7abd-5377-b1f0-9d3eafc436be" :answer-field/key "$A$ has $5$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460880}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f4e1182-d195-5cca-bb1a-601ea1f9c921" :question/math-academy-id "q-47599" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $7\\times 7$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{7} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=7=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=7,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $7$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{7}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d248bbb6-50b4-5d61-a95e-58f318131503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464246} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d0dfe-318f-5100-ac82-83455377b98c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d0dfe-318f-5100-ac82-83455377b98c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464247} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d37791a-a285-5a2f-af41-bcd2d8afc075" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465057} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3957e353-c39b-5011-af11-d2c9b6787af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} {:answer/id #uuid "8a540690-cbd6-5a7b-8e6a-735ce1ef7a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3957e353-c39b-5011-af11-d2c9b6787af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464248} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cfe4de2-b1c4-55bb-a60d-27c7be7257dc" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)<n$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f6788d6-5506-57b7-9972-0d793d0b67f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464250} {:answer/id #uuid "67197e1a-6b46-5a73-9b9e-21d0f7711026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67197e1a-6b46-5a73-9b9e-21d0f7711026" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464251} :answer-field/id #uuid "41d8c4a3-f095-50cd-bcf7-92ff6b429b75" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465059}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "795129ab-7204-5692-a97c-e32525213e2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142475" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{n} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, according to the invertible matrix theorem, \n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)<n.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$*  $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ is invertible”; $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a86c9ea-79e9-50fc-bc35-cf2fee7cdfed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} {:answer/id #uuid "8712eb23-d6cb-5de9-b4b0-12bf3d790d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a86c9ea-79e9-50fc-bc35-cf2fee7cdfed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464252} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ef167d-4bc6-5f6b-9cd2-3492c740a0f5" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465060} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6eae4da1-dd85-56d5-8efd-a6744dd9efb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} {:answer/id #uuid "915b008a-1011-5090-8324-7e9001f057b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eae4da1-dd85-56d5-8efd-a6744dd9efb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464254} :answer-field/id #uuid "b38b7760-7c88-5d50-8e1a-83c437c15443" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{16}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "952b73be-fa27-5c33-ac51-fe0f11cb7be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464256} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc948d7-8345-54f5-aac4-3efcd42070c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fc948d7-8345-54f5-aac4-3efcd42070c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464257} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6398a3-5006-54e1-b7af-c62ec5fc9eea" :answer-field/key "$A$ has $8$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465062}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7036dc73-9ca4-59f2-b983-11eaacfb5a4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142476" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{8} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has $8$ pivot columns” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d1fafe-67a4-5304-b42b-0fa34a95eaff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467578} {:answer/id #uuid "c76c9ea4-d5d0-5c09-adc5-db52b1568fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c76c9ea4-d5d0-5c09-adc5-db52b1568fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df948ff-c1ab-538f-b99e-ed07682677fc" :answer-field/key "$A$ has no inverse" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6428bf6c-1cd8-523e-89a2-bbd6aefca97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} {:answer/id #uuid "49e7f113-867c-5ee0-a738-ba5b88651827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6428bf6c-1cd8-523e-89a2-bbd6aefca97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8c77e6-a0b4-526b-bf8e-a435b7b66ac1" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=n$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b22f319-2182-5f2f-984d-2c69a38c95bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} {:answer/id #uuid "f8184f79-583b-5721-92be-e461d3dc1a14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b22f319-2182-5f2f-984d-2c69a38c95bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} :answer-field/id #uuid "d58f3fca-628f-5dd4-9837-348f91ad595e" :answer-field/key "All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468512}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c600e13-fdff-5526-82d0-6659ac10dfc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-47587" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times$\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has no inverse” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0038a274-1fea-5c60-93f2-4e1f0aa3d0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} {:answer/id #uuid "483dc84e-dfea-55fa-a0cb-de1ae000bf1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0038a274-1fea-5c60-93f2-4e1f0aa3d0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2201cc9-18d3-571c-ae72-347981af2222" :answer-field/key "$A$ is **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb16210a-cfa0-52ec-956b-46bc4659a344" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468246} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc5591d-8321-5239-af2f-da46eeeba04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cc5591d-8321-5239-af2f-da46eeeba04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0d4571-9f8e-5b3c-8a20-6f5a2b8194b8" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=n$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38651f09-b1dd-5820-93c3-99e2657a2fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468248} {:answer/id #uuid "3f51e910-74bd-5148-8e34-b3c363679221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f51e910-74bd-5148-8e34-b3c363679221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249} :answer-field/id #uuid "020dec00-eb40-52fb-acf8-97681452e138" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468845}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e25ee2d5-6236-5cb7-ae46-36798fde6f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-79334" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times$\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=n$; $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d5ed8d-7e60-5db5-b7d1-d96bb65185a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474362} {:answer/id #uuid "10b14067-3f7f-5868-8791-43396e0607b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10b14067-3f7f-5868-8791-43396e0607b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474363} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb207fd4-1ade-5c72-8528-ba143a738870" :answer-field/key "$A$ has no inverse" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0948d764-f192-5b49-80f0-17ce4b9bcefb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474364} {:answer/id #uuid "f2aade65-5d3a-520b-86ea-745a85070e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0948d764-f192-5b49-80f0-17ce4b9bcefb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474364} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b6ddd3-8ce7-5c7f-874e-23d5563021dc" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475108} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23dc218b-818c-594c-978b-8b69736909ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474366} {:answer/id #uuid "4999264b-817a-578e-85f5-209e47509eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4999264b-817a-578e-85f5-209e47509eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474367} :answer-field/id #uuid "25ecf0bb-4395-5d51-99bd-1c0a67d30176" :answer-field/key "$A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475109}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "251cfe7e-474d-59b2-8ccf-101401daf068" :question/math-academy-id "q-139978" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{5} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $det(A)=0,$ the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero.* $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn,  means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis so the dimension must be greater than zero.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))\\ne 5,$ which means that $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has no inverse”; “$A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446323} {:answer/id #uuid "6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} {:answer/id #uuid "65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446326} {:answer/id #uuid "720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446330} {:answer/id #uuid "f701af70-1e73-5b6a-b0c6-4b6e59b2fa9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446325} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd81b3b5-e497-5c05-9bc7-9bf55e4547fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-141215" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} {:answer/id #uuid "bd0f6e35-d7c3-5c27-95f6-6b6b01493577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446343} {:answer/id #uuid "d9adf053-ad3b-5a09-87f7-674bd680f4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446348} {:answer/id #uuid "db451e16-e9ec-50a7-a360-3e56d95fe251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446350} {:answer/id #uuid "f36d2201-ba87-5be6-b825-8ab2db34fb07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446324} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa1830b-5add-5daf-9fd3-0b3e06eb4a22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446362}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9326523-4bce-5554-9699-fb91223b9531" :question/math-academy-id "q-142479" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $A$ is invertible.* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$  then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ which means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ actually has a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible it must be $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446313} {:answer/id #uuid "2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446315} {:answer/id #uuid "41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446319} {:answer/id #uuid "662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446327} {:answer/id #uuid "a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446340} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446370}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec73c900-b909-5aa7-beeb-5f5b6ee2fba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141341" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $det(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then we must have $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$*  $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d885553-3afc-5696-a382-4c860965f60c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528520} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf00a72-f79f-582d-9aaa-38874ff20b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528592} {:answer/id #uuid "7df12baa-7b1b-58dc-8f63-3871724e61dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528598} {:answer/id #uuid "c974d506-c2bc-5e7b-97a4-c51ae5371031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528794} {:answer/id #uuid "e94c076f-c6c7-517d-8c55-d74158a4a6fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d885553-3afc-5696-a382-4c860965f60c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528520} :answer-field/id #uuid "20580d7d-28aa-5c7c-a048-784d0bfa2d4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528956}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1d7f6a4-6114-5671-a52c-7df48bee5e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-141342" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately. \n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn, means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we must have that $A$ is **not** invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n},$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04c50643-01aa-57fa-8703-551f411bcef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616382} {:answer/id #uuid "341e787a-6216-56d1-addd-83742093725f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616459} {:answer/id #uuid "bc33d81e-9442-5b3d-9e29-5ebf4f6366a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616713} {:answer/id #uuid "d5396c66-36ca-5609-9c8e-2f99af1e2e6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616758} {:answer/id #uuid "e3317a2c-6551-5c55-9f93-e3277b68058b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3317a2c-6551-5c55-9f93-e3277b68058b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616775} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d03ec9-bb33-5a1b-9a2d-866361f6881e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616852}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a20e0f6e-9a4b-59f0-b28f-3a10b5209120" :question/math-academy-id "q-141205" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns\n\nIII. $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the matrix $A$ must be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\},$ which means that $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217d00e3-6085-5217-9e0f-bc0ed267a659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627152} {:answer/id #uuid "4d216911-9fdd-5d94-9372-99c99ec03e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627226} {:answer/id #uuid "c69e47ba-4ae4-5ccc-94e3-da31c8bee3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627431} {:answer/id #uuid "cb083657-c6c3-5e24-8fd7-4d2f8e37c426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627440} {:answer/id #uuid "d61c0f82-de33-5eb0-80d0-e768ca91585e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb083657-c6c3-5e24-8fd7-4d2f8e37c426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627440} :answer-field/id #uuid "5be541ef-8f3c-5ccd-a814-640b71ca741c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627583}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48e66ecf-d81b-50c1-a8a1-a9e2ad76a682" :question/math-academy-id "q-141217" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ is not invertible, which means $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e0fc9f-7385-5c7b-ae3b-103b9330e3c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627091} {:answer/id #uuid "1c378646-9302-5a64-9728-c1b51529df79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627145} {:answer/id #uuid "708def97-75ed-58ef-a2bf-6861c83ab912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627282} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8fd432-6f8f-51c7-bfbb-559a7ea21b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627354} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c36613-e9d3-5ba7-91ca-a44714c54624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00e0fc9f-7385-5c7b-ae3b-103b9330e3c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627091} :answer-field/id #uuid "48b9389d-612d-5d40-ba4a-42e4e4c73b9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627573}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "624ebabe-0dfa-5173-b265-5c678170209c" :question/math-academy-id "q-142478" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nIII. $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\},$ which means that $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186662343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb0df87-6b66-5944-b1dd-454ba552f9db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661659} {:answer/id #uuid "228b7b0a-3160-5b2a-b1d1-61d079480a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661678} {:answer/id #uuid "314661e8-5e45-5943-b8e5-9fcd7ab80791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661704} {:answer/id #uuid "34d03e7e-d18b-5ca3-92b3-37a181e42b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661714} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9f293d-624e-5ed9-913e-8cb4be3d342c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bb0df87-6b66-5944-b1dd-454ba552f9db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661659} :answer-field/id #uuid "f75f7499-83c9-59af-ba8f-207dccb35553" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186662249}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dae4fbb5-bcbf-541b-9afd-ea52e3dddf91" :question/math-academy-id "q-47604" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))\\le n-1\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ the matrix $A$ can have at most  $n-1$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186662344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "410d25ee-90ba-563c-943d-db4052119c78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661739} {:answer/id #uuid "946260af-9902-5d47-9925-fbe161873cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661880} {:answer/id #uuid "9d18bcd5-71b2-5b84-bee1-7f8b1aefb062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661898} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f069db-9ecb-576b-a1d9-18ecf527a428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661962} {:answer/id #uuid "cb788b15-b090-5bb3-9a67-25e175ed8608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6f069db-9ecb-576b-a1d9-18ecf527a428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186661962} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1fe6272-f996-503c-bc14-a61bb015472a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186662247}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db5a5ae3-0add-50b7-955f-ff73e4e003cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-141214" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince $det(A)=0,$ it must be $Ax=0$ has non-trivial solution, which means $\\text{Null}(A)$ has basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n}.$*$\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, $A$ is not invertible because $det(A)=0.$  Since $A$ is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n}.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$*  $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $det(A)=0,$ then $Ax=0$ has non-trivial solution, which means that $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b93aa7-c591-5841-aa3a-357d8bf16eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673116} {:answer/id #uuid "45cde434-4d75-5c09-9b0f-35b920274076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673121} {:answer/id #uuid "52405711-96a4-58b9-b20b-772647cc4c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673122} {:answer/id #uuid "70a7bdca-b802-5569-bfd3-d23438559962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673127} {:answer/id #uuid "cddf6d9c-c0bf-57b1-b126-0839ec3bed59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15b93aa7-c591-5841-aa3a-357d8bf16eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673116} :answer-field/id #uuid "e61f64c2-6321-5d18-9115-5e8492b4d1ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673145}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24f7a599-64fa-59b0-bc94-5119ac1b11b5" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $\\operatorname{Col}(A)\\subsetneq\\mathbb{R}^{n}$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* ×\n\nEvery finite-dimensional subspace has a basis. The zero subspace has the empty basis.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{Col}(A)\\subsetneq\\mathbb{R}^{n}$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e0c05b-14aa-5e14-b955-527ebc07ec4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673113} {:answer/id #uuid "3b0d39f6-4254-5d22-bf4e-6febe4ad2533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b0d39f6-4254-5d22-bf4e-6febe4ad2533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673119} :answer-field/id #uuid "956051b9-5768-5547-88b9-3b7e942076a5" :answer-field/key "$\\det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "348adaf6-7787-565e-9ff4-1f701aa97384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673118} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5e628e-f4dc-5d13-9581-7e8bb52ecd66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "348adaf6-7787-565e-9ff4-1f701aa97384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673118} :answer-field/id #uuid "987163a9-96d8-5ed7-b484-24cd137c96e9" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c0ef31-2044-5855-a7a9-cab2011298ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673115} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a583d1-5c19-57bb-b0b1-2de813730ab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14c0ef31-2044-5855-a7a9-cab2011298ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673115} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d31553-b93e-5bf7-a7e6-04e42a08a1de" :answer-field/key "$A$ has fewer than $7$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673143}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "635f4b7d-7d59-52ae-8c0d-6343e80d6951" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{7}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=7=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $\\det(A)=0$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=7$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\det(A)\\ne 0$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=7$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$, then $A$ has fewer than $7$ pivot columns.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=7$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ has $7$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{7}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81068501-c0e2-5f32-acb0-2aace6ed6c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673132} {:answer/id #uuid "99a5c457-06a2-52cc-aa45-339994a36685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81068501-c0e2-5f32-acb0-2aace6ed6c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673132} :answer-field/id #uuid "01abd1c7-c59f-5c99-9277-f9537d6b88ca" :answer-field/key "$A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d553a7c-18de-5cec-850b-80701a20b3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673123} {:answer/id #uuid "9001b869-f87a-5bff-81cb-628feb2d2463" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d553a7c-18de-5cec-850b-80701a20b3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673123} :answer-field/id #uuid "752229c8-1a98-538b-b81c-a0f7d16e0605" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1045ca11-00a7-54f5-82df-d90677220306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673114} {:answer/id #uuid "987039ff-1afd-51f5-acdd-306be4aaac88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "987039ff-1afd-51f5-acdd-306be4aaac88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673136} :answer-field/id #uuid "970549a2-6eb7-57d6-af88-f32a52d1299f" :answer-field/key "$A$ is **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a51a92b7-4da1-53a7-a184-875247f5a8f5" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $A$ is **not** invertible.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A$ has $n$ pivot columns."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040ad0ff-3100-5425-b2f1-da7e669a2b4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673112} {:answer/id #uuid "4238513f-e322-530e-9565-e1ef6525b9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673120} {:answer/id #uuid "756e0384-4d12-5af5-b55c-3d54c0e1e087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673130} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c55ca2-2506-540d-8b37-d903917854aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673142} {:answer/id #uuid "f803c880-b273-55c6-86f9-5f9ae0631781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4238513f-e322-530e-9565-e1ef6525b9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673120} :answer-field/id #uuid "64adbc10-22f8-5b06-93cc-be533f313081" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673125}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ece9d320-1fda-5bca-bfdf-852dee2b03f3" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, then $A$ is **not** invertible.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$. Thus $A$ is **not** invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, then $\\det(A)=0$.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$. Thus $\\det(A)=0$.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$. Thus $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I and II only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cf403e2-fc73-51e8-93ac-21bd4fa4deb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673126} {:answer/id #uuid "735ac19d-aa52-5baf-a48d-1b36bd66de03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673128} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa16602-e7c9-54cd-a27f-713bd6b96dc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673131} {:answer/id #uuid "9b066337-30b7-5051-a050-f4cc7caba6b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673139} {:answer/id #uuid "f20ce81b-8827-55b8-8eda-03664eee7b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f20ce81b-8827-55b8-8eda-03664eee7b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673149} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7a0c1cc-ebfa-5947-959b-5472ae9f3909" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673146}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f57a7c6f-101e-5b33-aef0-c7309a1bc9ae" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}A\\text{ is invertible}\\\\\\Updownarrow\\\\\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{n}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A))&=n=\\operatorname{rank}(A)\\\\\\operatorname{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\}\\\\\\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A))&=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\operatorname{rank}(A)<n$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)>0$.* ×\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* ✓\n\nThe given condition implies $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=n$ and $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=0$. Thus $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III only."}] :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}]}
